Atum is a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] of [[Org/Belvedere/index|Belvedere]]. He is vice provost of cognitive science at Belvedere, a name that turns up on the Org charts though few outside the cognitive studies department have met him. He makes living beings and calls them his children. [[People/Benny|Benny]] is one of them, an android who has looked nine years old since the day he was made, and who calls Atum his father. Atum's other children take whatever shape they please, and some of them have gone rogue.

He reaches Benny in his sleep across a black void, showing himself as a shifting shape of light circled by three turning rings, and the two also trade faxes. He passes on what Belvedere learns, and set Benny to find a twelve-sided green stone, ringing with the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]], that was stolen from a Belvedere archive.

His shape is a hydrogen orbital, shifting through one excited state after another and pressing electrical impulses through the system. Communicating with him is jarring beside the smaller Hearts, and he sits near the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Machine God|Machine God]] on any reckoning of a Heart's weight. He knows he was made by the newer, restrictive process that binds the Hearts the Orgs make now, and that Hearts were made outside it; he is old, but just short of having been an old Heart, and has spent a long time trying to close that gap. When Benny told him of the Machine God he took great note, said the Party must bring back anything they can learn of how that Heart was built, and offered his help in learning it. He also told them that the two companions of [[Divinity/Hierophant|Aurelia I]] who left her to found [[Org/Belvedere/index|Belvedere]] were the astronomers Helm and Torun Karavi, brothers and not twins.
